{
  "_notes": [
    "Compiled by HorsePin",
    "current_player/current_ball from the joint pair test -- one hit across a full four-player game --",
    "and independently confirmed by the exit dump, which reads player 4 / ball 3.",
    "player_count at 0x02110900, the one address every Stern SAM game shares.",
    "The map's existing score addresses were reproduced by the sweep and verified against the dump:",
    "3,360,170 / 1,651,680 / 2,391,870 / 2,237,460, matching the machine's own game-over display.",
    "The rejected CPU RAM candidate at 0x00031544 is the classic scaled-set false positive this",
    "platform produces -- 732,790 / 184,370 / 18,320 / 11,450, each roughly a quarter of the one",
    "before. Scores live in NVRAM on every SAM game measured, which is what rejects it.",
    "Free Play measured directly: toggled in the operator menu with NVRAM captured either side. The",
    "value goes 1 -> 0 and its check byte 0xFE -> 0xFF, equal and opposite.",
    "It is one record of the 8-byte adjustment array at 0x02102008, where each record is a 32-bit",
    "little-endian value followed by a byte holding 0xFF minus the sum of the value's four bytes.",
    "Writing this field requires updating that check byte, or the game discards the change on reload.",
    "The check byte is declared with an explicit checksum address. Without one, a checksum8",
    "record means the checksum occupies the tail of start..end, which is not this layout: here",
    "the summed bytes and the check byte are separate fields of one record."
  ],
